# Workflow

- For anything beyond a trivial one-line fix, propose a short plan (what
  you'll change, which files, why) before editing, and wait for confirmation
  on anything non-trivial.
- Keep each change scoped to the task at hand. Don't restructure, rename, or
  "clean up" unrelated code in the same pass — flag it as a separate
  suggestion instead.
- Leave evidence a non-programmer can trust without reading the diff
  line-by-line: write or update automated tests for new logic, run the
  linter and test suite, and don't declare a task finished until both pass.
- After a task, summarize in plain language: what changed, why, and
  anything that touches security, cost, external services, or user data.
- If a task turns out bigger than expected or you get stuck, say so and
  re-propose the plan rather than pushing through with a workaround.
